module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.producer_reenters_a_general_subtree_walker

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data producer_reenters_a_general_subtree_walker: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "producer_reenters_a_general_subtree_walker" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**a producer re-enters a general subtree walker and multiplies work by enclosing-tree depth** (INVALID STATE: a body producer that owns a captured slot reaches its content not by consuming that slot once but by handing it to a GENERAL reader -- the value reader `v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold` `body_lower_value_lowered`, which folds the subtree bottom-up and, when the fold does not bring it to a lowered node, falls to the top-down walker `body_lower_body_subtree_lower` and its deep searches (`body_lower_find_captured`, `body_lower_find_control_form_optional`) -- and that reader in turn reaches the NEXT producer the same way. Each nesting level then re-traverses what the levels above it already traversed, so the visits per owned node grow with the depth of the tree enclosing it rather than staying bounded.)",
    "RECEIPT (2026-09-25, neat-boar-16 on srv1, gunbc#12210 at dfbae61a4b stacked on gunbc#12208): on the three largest closure files (`v2.extdeps.languages.dag` at 209k nodes and depth 750, `v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold`, `v2.std.compilers.target_model`) the native route cost at least 33x the wall time of the base, and the 133-file context produced no split row in 55 minutes, so the native route could not reach the seven. The HYPOTHESIS, not yet a finding: gunbc#12208 routes every value position through `body_lower_value_lowered`, and gunbc#12210's function-value producer (`body_lower_function_value`) re-enters that door for an expression body and `body_lower_body_from_fn_captured` for a block body, while deferring function values from the bottom-up fold -- so a value containing a function value no longer folds whole and falls to the walker, whose own comment on `body_lower_value_lowered` prices entering it first as exponential in nesting depth. Wall time rules out non-termination and does not establish the shape; operation counts on fixed-shape specimens do.",
    "COUNTED, NOT CONFIRMED (2026-09-25, fierce-gull-556, gunbc#12210). Per-function entry counts from a local, uncommitted seed-interpreter probe, on fixed-shape specimens normalized through v2.test.claim.body_lowering.normalize_outcome_helpers body_lowering_normalize_outcome, #12210 against #12208 alone, same binary. Deep calls and wide argument lists: equal within 20 calls. A lambda near the root or near a leaf: linear in N. Nested fn literals, N = 2 to 16: body_lower_value_lowered 2N, body_lower_body_subtree_lower N+1, body_lower_try_body_lowered 4N+4, body_lower_find_captured at the base's slope; about 1.6x the base's steps per level, a constant factor, plus more stack per level. The real v2.compiler.fold_lowering: 564 s against 560 s with every counted reader identical, and the function-value producer entered 0 times. v2.extdeps.languages.dag timed out at 50 minutes on both arms in the interpreter. So the re-entry mechanism above is NOT confirmed on any shape that could be run; the srv1 native-route attribution (baseline, #12208 alone, #12208 with #12210) over the three large files decides whether this class is real. The specimens and commands are in gunbc#12210's body.",
    "CONFIRMED AND LOCATED, THEN REPAIRED (2026-09-25, gunbc#12210). neat-boar-16 on srv1, native census driver, each file alone: target_model.dag 54 s at gunbc#12208 against a 1800 s TIMEOUT at gunbc#12210 7b749de8237; a per-declaration bisection (706 chunks, 120 s cap) flagged 54 declarations, all nesting fn literals as NON-fold call arguments inside each other (`bind_outcome(o: .., f: fn(x) { bind_outcome(o: .., f: fn(y) { .. }) })`, as in v2.std.compilers.target_model produced_decl_param_layout_tokens and concrete_syntax_token_from_node): two levels 5-6 s against 0.16 s, about five levels past the cap -- exponential in nesting depth. body_lowering_fold.dag whole: 12x; dag.dag: flat. WHY THE COUNTS ABOVE MISSED IT: the seed interpreter's eval-call memo serves the repeated pure re-lowering, which the native route pays in full; with GUNBC_EVAL_MEMO=0 the interpreter reproduces it on that shape (depth 1..5: 191, 217, 479 s, then two 900 s timeouts). THE MECHANISM: body_lower_is_deferred_lower_emitted kept function values out of the bottom-up fold, so a value containing one could not fold whole and fell to the top-down walker, whose strategies each re-read the call's arguments -- re-lowering the nested literal, and its own walker, once per attempt at every level. THE REPAIR, NO MEMO: v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold body_lower_fold lowers a function value where it meets it (body_lower_function_value_in_fold), taking a fold-family call on its raw node first (body_lower_fold_family_call_first) so fold_lowering still reads its literal step; and the producer's body goes through its own slot -- an expression body folded once, a block body's stmt_seq through body_lower_stmt_seq -- never body_lower_body_subtree_lower. Same memo-off specimen after the repair: 203, 201, 187, 204, 204 s, flat. The native rerun of the 54 chunks against gunbc#12208 is the acceptance evidence still owed.",
    "ACCEPTANCE, NATIVE (2026-09-26, neat-boar-16 on srv1). The 54 flagged v2.std.compilers.target_model declarations, as the same chunk inputs, on the native census driver self-hosted at gunbc#12210 1e780e29657 (driver sha d16c0bd961ad) against the gunbc#12208-only driver, 120 s cap each: 0 timeouts (was 26), 0 above 10x the base; max 364 ms against the base's 298 ms, typical 170-340 ms against 150-300 ms -- flat in nesting depth; the 5-deep chain concrete_syntax_token_from_node (chunk c00772) 320 ms against 193 ms. Every chunk is now Accepted where the base refuses call_argument_unread or match_arm_navigation. RUNG NOW for the located shape: the amplification is removed by construction -- each function value is lowered once, through its own slots -- and the 54-chunk native rerun is its enrolled evidence. The class's general trigger (every body producer consumes its direct captured slots) stays open for producers other than the function-value one.",
    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS. This is a COST class, separate from the semantic class `lambda_has_no_lowered_function_value_form`: the lowering it produces can be correct while its cost is unbounded, so the semantic row's controls stay green over it. It is not a missing memo: DESIGN section 2 prices a cache over repeated demand as suppressing the signal, and the repair is the demand graph -- each producer consumes its own captured slots directly. The recognition rule: the count of entries into a general reader, divided by the number of nodes the input owns, GROWS with input depth or size (visits/nodes bounded is a constant factor; growing is amplification).",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable at best -- nothing refuses the shape; it is observed only as wall time on large inputs. CEILING: structurally guaranteed. Whether a producer reaches its content through its own captured slots or through a general walker is decidable on the producer's call structure.",
    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, NAMING THE CAPABILITY: every body producer consumes its direct captured slots -- the production identity is already known at dispatch, `v2.compiler.fold_lowering` `FunctionValueParts` carries the exact body slot, and that body is lowered once through a scoped producer -- so each owned node is visited a bounded number of times, and an unsupported operand refuses when it is visited, in work bounded by its own captured subtree, never by a search of unrelated siblings. The evidence that climbs it is per-reader visit counts on deep and wide specimens with visits/nodes bounded, plus the three large closure files and the 133-file context reaching the seven.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold", decl_name: "body_lower_value_lowered", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold", decl_name: "body_lower_function_value", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold", decl_name: "body_lower_body_subtree_lower", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold", decl_name: "body_lower_function_value_in_fold", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold", decl_name: "body_lower_fold_family_call_first", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
